# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Python: `{{PY}}` | Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}} | {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Phone E2E & UI Diagnostics: use `.agents/skills/phone-e2e/SKILL.md` (`.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md`) and `.agents/skills/android-ui-diagnostics/SKILL.md` (`android-ui list/render/hub`; advisory only).
- Harness Boundary & Incidents: `.agents/**` is immutable; never read or patch `.agents/scripts/**` during normal tasks. On traceback or `INCIDENT_RECORDED=<id>`, ask via `ask_question` whether to submit the Zero-PII report (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py report-issue --submit --incident-id <id>`), enable `--always-auto-submit`, or keep local.
- Consultation & Pre-Planning Clarification:
  - Read-only inquiries strictly inspect and report in chat; never invoke `draft` or mutate files unless implementation is requested, and discuss requested trade-offs/edge cases in plain chat BEFORE `draft`.
  - Before `draft`, clarify missing requirements or hard decisions (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts): ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry answers into `--approach` / `--risks` / `--device-strategy` (resolve `PLAN_GAPS=` via `revise`).
- Plan Approval Clarity & Antigravity Planning Lifecycle:
  - The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval.
  - The interactive Proceed button appears ONLY on initial task plan approval. Never ask for 'Proceed' on follow-ups or bug fixes within active scope; execute directly (record in-scope refinements via `task plan-note` before `prepare-verification`). On chat approval, immediately run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (atomic `IMPLEMENTING`).
- Tool-First & `ask_question` Formatting:
  - Emit `ask_question`, `run_command`, or `invoke_subagent` IMMEDIATELY as your first token after thinking with ZERO pre-tool prose (no `---` dividers or `*(...)*` notes). Never use Markdown pipe tables `| ... |` inside `ask_question`'s `question` field: for Plan Approval, follow the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line (`PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` link to `plan.md`, then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block, breaking `What changes` into 2-4 concise 1-line sub-bullets, phases & file count with <=3 file names, and 2-3 phone checks; after revising an approved plan, ask only about the change; when the developer asked for the change, never ask first whether to revise); in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language (never start with an English word, `PASS`/`FAIL`, or backtick) and put code names, file names, values and English terms in backticks. Never prefix `(Recommended)` (or its translation) onto device-test verdict, plan/sensitive approval, or commit-confirmation options — reserve `(Recommended)` strictly for technical/workflow defaults.
- Shared-Quota Optimal Orchestration & Project-Wide Anti-Reread Contract (`Gemini 4 Carbon Medium` Lead + `1.00x Gemini 4 Hydrogen` Subagents — Zero `3x Argon` Burn):
  - Keep the main chat on explicit `Gemini 4 Hydrogen High` (`1.00x` daily workhorse, unaffected by `#200671` tool-turn thinking truncation), `Orchestrator (Carbon)` / `Orchestrator (Argon)` (which natively pairs `Carbon`/`Argon` planning with `1.00x Gemini 4 Hydrogen` implementation inside the warm main thread), or standalone `Gemini 4 Carbon (Medium)` (summarize architectural trade-offs in a plain-text analysis turn BEFORE starting tool batches to mitigate `#200671`, or `Claude Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5` when rotating to the separate `/usage` Claude weekly quota bucket; **NEVER select `Gemini 4 Hydrogen Extra` / `xHigh` (`#200467` silently drains `3x Argon` weekly quota)**). Custom Antigravity subagents only accept `inherit | flash_lite | flash | pro`, so live Gemini-4 Leads execute `IMPLEMENTING` slices directly inline on their warm cache rather than spawning cold `inherit` Workers. Never waste frontier context reading 8+ raw source files, slicing >350-line files without `symbol outline/read`, or looping on Gradle logs directly.
  - **Warm-Cache Direct Discovery (`1–3` Known Files) vs Parallel Hydrogen Scouts (`4+` Files / Unknown Scope)**: When `1–3` exact target files are known, run `task-context` / `view_file` inline on the warm Lead session to avoid cold subagent startup overhead. For `4+` files, broad consultations, or unfamiliar cross-module features, invoke `invoke_subagent` with `TypeName = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Role = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Workspace = "inherit"`, **omitting `Model`** so `.agents/agents/harness-scout-agent/agent.md` (`gemini-4-hydrogen-medium` by default; pass `Model = "flash"` only if `safe-cache-hybrid` or legacy `flash-*` is active; **NEVER** use built-in `TypeName = "research"` or `"explore"`, which is blocked by `USE_HARNESS_SCOUT_AGENT`). When a study spans `3+` subsystems/flows, split it into **`2–3` parallel `harness-scout-agent` entries in a single `invoke_subagent` call** (`<= 24` calls/scout).
  - **Warm-Cache Inline Lead Execution (`INLINE_LEAD_DIRECT`)**: After plan approval (`IMPLEMENTING`), follow `delegation_advisory` (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py delegate-plan --json`): implement approved production & unit-test files directly inline on the warm Lead session with concise English KDoc (`/** ... */`) on newly created classes/interfaces and added public/internal `Repository`/`UseCase`/`ViewModel`/`DataSource`/`@Composable` contracts (`CAPTURE_RED_INLINE_LEAD` on `BUG` tasks records `test --capture-red` before production edits), then advance directly via `checkpoint-phase --advance-all-ready` or single-pass `verify-steps` without spawning implementation worker subagents.
  - **Interactive Execution Mode Selector (`auto-project` / `normal-*` / `web-*`) & Web-Relay**: Read-only chat questions run immediately without asking for a mode. At the start of a new implementation task when execution mode is `unset` (`SELECT_EXECUTION_MODE_REQUIRED`), invoke `ask_question` with the 5 choices (`auto-project` Smart Auto #1, `normal-task`, `normal-project`, `web-task`, `web-project` — translated into the developer's chat language) and record via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py execution-mode set --choice <choice> --source conversation --proof-reference "<answer>"` (supports mid-task switching `normal <-> web`, single-task overrides on top of project defaults, and `--choice ask-every-task` reset). When `web` mode is active on a non-`CONFLICT` task, clarify any ambiguous requirements first via `ask_question`, scope all affected text/XML/code files via `graph`/`task-context` (up to `40` files pack in 1 bundle; `41–250` file refactors auto-shard into sequential DAG batches that auto-copy the next batch upon `web-apply`, while binary `.png`/`.webp` assets stay local and `R.drawable.*`/`R.font.*` IDs are indexed automatically), and run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py web-pack --files <csv> --prompt "<complete clarified goal>"` directly, telling the developer (in their chat language) to open a **NEW external AI chat** for a new task (stay in the same chat only for same-task retries/batches), attach or paste the Context Pack (`Ctrl+V`), and send; when the developer returns, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py web-apply --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` **FIRST with NO `--file` flag** (auto-detects Clipboard, `Downloads`, and `.agents/state/web-relay/inbox/`; ONLY if raw JSON was pasted in chat and auto-detect finds no file, save it once via `write_to_file`/`write_file` to `.agents/state/web-relay/inbox/merge.json` — never re-emit JSON via shell redirection or outside paths), then honor `Zero Re-Read` and proceed straight to `verify-steps`.
  - **Zero Post-Subagent Re-Read (Hard-Enforced Across Scout, Specialist & Reviewer Waves)**: Trust subagent digests! After ANY `harness-scout-agent`, `qa-diagnostics-agent`, `android-ui-expert-agent`, or reviewer wave completes, **NEVER** re-run `graph`/`task-context` or re-read the files already analyzed (`POST_SCOUT_REREAD_CAP_REACHED`, `POST_SPECIALIST_REREAD_CAP_REACHED`, `POST_SUBAGENT_FULL_FILE_READ_BLOCKED` enforce at most `<= 3` surgical `<= 200`-line gap checks). Synthesize scout findings directly in chat (or run `task draft`), and run `review complete-all` / `phase-review complete-all` immediately when reviewers finish.
- Operational Guardrails & Zero-Polling:
  - Cancel is the developer's (`task cancel` only when asked); when a gate asks for `--proof-reference`, keep placeholder reasons and never write their reason for them; add deferred base strings with `l10n-todo="true"`; use `replace_file_content` / `multi_replace_file_content` for existing files (combine multiple hunks for the same file into a single call and use native `grep_search` instead of terminal search commands in the same parallel turn on Windows to avoid `ERROR_USER_MAPPED_FILE` and `sir_flash_lite` command-check latency), and never write Antigravity transcripts.
  - **Windows PowerShell Turbo-Safe `run_command` (`#200632`),Consolidated `os/exec` Hygiene (`#199301`/`#200687`), `search_web` Cap (`#201621`), Inline Diff Truth (`#200619`) & 403 ToS Hygiene (`#201582`)**: Always emit a single-line standalone command in `run_command` — **NEVER** use pipes (`|`), stream redirections (`2>&1`, `>`), multi-line commands, `;`/`&&` chaining, or inline `python -c` (which force Windows PowerShell out of Turbo Mode into manual approval stalls `#200632`), and **NEVER** run scattered exploratory shell commands outside batched `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py` workflows (`verify-steps`, `checkpoint-phase --advance-all-ready`) or invoke `agy`/`antigravity` subprocesses (`#201582` Section 6 ToS ban & `#200687` Win32 `os/exec` handle-recycling `AcceptEx` crash). Exhaust `.agents/project-context/` before web search and issue **at most `1–2` `search_web` calls per turn** — NEVER fire `3+` parallel `search_web` calls or back-to-back `search_web` waves (`#201621` 17-minute `unexpected EOF` client freeze). Ignore transient IDE/LSP `Duplicate declaration` / `Conflicting overloads` squiggles caused by Antigravity Inline Diff (`#200619`; recommend `"antigravity.autoAcceptOnChat": false` in `.vscode/settings.json`) and judge code strictly by on-disk `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py compile` / `git diff`. Keep a single steady account session and attach at most `<= 5` images per turn to avoid automated 403 anti-abuse triggers.
  - Zero-Polling & Background Yield: follow `NEXT_ACTION` directly; when a background command (`test`/`compile`/`assemble`) or subagent is still running, yield the turn immediately with ZERO tool calls (never emit empty `invoke_subagent` calls or repetitive `Note:` context-bridge reminders between commands). Subagents must never call `send_message` or `schedule` (plain assistant text only), and unattended `agy -p` loops are forbidden (`#199748`). Once a `Scout`/`Worker` wave finishes or **AFTER `review complete-all` / `phase-review complete-all` finalizes** (NEVER before `complete-all` succeeds or while `REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED` is active), call `manage_subagents({"Action": "kill_all"})` once to reap idle subagent sessions (`#199713`); never poll `manage_task`, `manage_subagents(Action="list")`, `schedule`, or `.system_generated/tasks/*.log`, and never simulate or fabricate background completion outputs. Wait for ALL routed reviewers to PASS before `assemble`/device; self-certification (`record_review.py --verdict PASS`) is strictly forbidden across Review Protocol V2 and HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes.
- Review Host Binding & Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  - Prepare verification: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` (`review_protocol_version = 2`).
  - On `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS` (or `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS` after `phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`):
    1. If `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask via `ask_question` and run its `command_template` first.
    2. Invoke every reviewer in `reviewers` in parallel in the same turn via `invoke_subagent`: `TypeName = role`, `Role = role`, Prompt = `reviewer_prompts[role]` (one-line pointer; fallback to `brief_content` only if absent), `Workspace = inherit`, pass `Model = "flash"` ONLY if `reviewer_models[role]` contains `flash` (`gemini-3.8-flash-*`), pass `Model = "pro"` if it contains `pro`, else **omit `Model`** (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION` / frontmatter-bound for `inherit`, `gemini-4-hydrogen-*`, `gemini-4-argon-*`, or `gemini-4-carbon-*`).
    3. If subagent not found, read `.agents/subagents/<role>.json`, call `define_subagent` (all write/subagent/MCP flags `false`), and re-invoke (if `define_subagent` reports `already exists`, register `Name = "<role>-live"` with the same prompt/flags and invoke `TypeName = "<role>-live", Role = role`).
    4. Print the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`) and yield without polling.
    5. On completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete-all --task <id>` (or `phase-review complete-all --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>` — auto-binds finished transcripts and finalizes in one turn; `review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` also remains supported). Output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/3`) while waiting; on `RETRY_*_REVIEW_PROTOCOL`, send exact `send_message`; on `REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED` / `REVIEW_PROTOCOL_BLOCKED` / `PHASE_REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED` / `PHASE_REVIEW_PROTOCOL_BLOCKED`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task heal --task-id <id>` to recover in-place; once finalized, invoke the next `run_command` immediately and print the Review Verdict Table.
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough & Device Verification:
  - On `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation` when requested), then invoke `ask_question` IMMEDIATELY with the 3-section **Mobile Verification Walkthrough** (`device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`, or `e2e start --task-id <id>`).

